From 4d50970c48b358959f4411526e3d6cbaa7e6d1d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:11:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the preconditioners of the sparse matrices of MFEM, KLU
 and OrthoSolver

The Gauss-Seidel and Jacobi smoothers of the sparse matrices of MFEM
(GSSmoother, DSmoother), its block ILU(0) factorization (BlockILU) and
the direct solvers of SuiteSparse (UMFPack, KLU) are registered as
preconditioners, and KLU as the KLUSolver direct solver in sequential.
They are applied to the sparse matrix in sequential and to the diagonal
block of each process in parallel (block Jacobi method), through a
wrapper which gives them a copy of the matrix on the host only and
copies of the vectors on the host: mfem::KLUSolver and mfem::BlockILU
read the memory of the host without synchronizing it with the device
(wrong results with --device cuda before), and the matrix of mfem-mgis
or of hypre is no longer sorted in place. A singular matrix makes KLU
fail on all the processes (MFEM does not check its status).

The OrthoSolver preconditioner wraps another preconditioner and
orthogonalizes the vectors to the constant vector, on the host, for the
operators whose kernel is the constant vector.

UMFPackSolver and KLUSolver refuse unknown options.
